   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "וּבִלְבַד שֶׁתְּהֵא כְּתוּבָּתָהּ כּוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — אִשָּׁה הִקְנוּ לוֹ מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: The «only» exception to this is «that» her «marriage contract will» still «be» payable from the property of her first husband and not from the property of the yavam. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? The Gemara explains: «A wife was acquired to him by Heaven,» and since he did not choose her as a wife, he did not obligate himself to pay her marriage contract."
  }
